      "text": [
        " هُوَ وَ اللَّهِ عَلِيُّ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ ( عليه السلام ) ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad Bin Mihran, from Muhammad Bin Ali, from Abu Abdullah Al Sammat, from Yahya Bin Masawir, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Ja’far<sup>asws</sup>. This Verse was mentioned <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:9#h105\"><a href=\"/books/quran:9#h105\">[9:105]</a></a> And say: Work; so Allah will See your work and (so will) His Rasool and the Believers</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘He<sup>asws</sup>, by Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, is Ali<sup>asws</sup> Bin Abu Talib<sup>asws</sup>’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 5. Ahmad ibn Mahran has narrated from Muhammad ibn Ali from abu ‘Abdallah al-Samit from Yahya ibn Musawwir who has said the following. He mentioned this verse to abu Ja‘far (a.s.), “Act as you wish. God will see your deeds and so will do His Messenger and the believers. . .” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:9#h106\"><a href=\"/books/quran:9#h106\">[9:106]</a></a> The Imams (a.s.) then said, “I swear by Allah that he (the believer) is Ali ibn abu Talib (a.s.).”"
        ]
      }
    },
